{"abstract":"Reinforcement learning (RL) is a type of active learning whereby an agent learns to act in an environment by interacting with it. RL has applications in many domains, including robotics, gaming, electronics, healthcare, water management systems, etc. The majority of real-world applications of RL, such as those in robotics, necessitate a preliminary training phase in a simulation environment. It is otherwise either infeasible or prohibitively expensive to train the agent in a real-world setting. At the same time, there are clear advantages to be gained from the use of formal methods for the enhancement of software qualities. Given that RL and its applications are computer programs, the objective of this thesis is to employ formal methods, in particular pecification, testing, and symbolic execution, in order to improve the reliability and explainability of reinforcement learning.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ghaffari, Mohsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798548"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"testing and symbolic analysis for reinforcement learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109069093/Testing_and_Symbolic_Analysis_For_Reinforcement_Learning_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798548","ids":["itu-986f0d0d-dc4b-45e1-a619-f1e522bb8422"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FDD29D134631363B872C407D03922808"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109069093/Testing_and_Symbolic_Analysis_For_Reinforcement_Learning_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","locid":"c12518ce-b3ab-469c-81fb-e2178e6b87e3","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","orcid":"0000-0002-1939-9053","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779495319"],"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"233","pages":"192","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-986f0d0d-dc4b-45e1-a619-f1e522bb8422"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Testing and Symbolic Analysis For Reinforcement Learning","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798548","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This paper addresses the challenges posed by urban stormwater runoff in light of increased urbanization and climate change, which strain traditional stormwater infrastructure. It focuses on mitigating Combined Sewer Overflows (CSOs) by maximizing urban runoff storage in stormwater tunnels during Wastewater Treatment Plant (WWTP) capacity overloads. Unlike passive rule-based control, this research explores adaptive control systems that utilize weather forecasts and dynamic strategies. It introduces a novel control synthesis approach, combining Model Predictive Control (MPC) and Q-learning, to optimize CSO management based on real-time weather predictions. Simulated evaluations (using EPA-SWMM, focused on the Hvidovre stormwater tunnel in Copenhagen, Denmark) show significant improvements in CSO management: 17% over classic Q-learning and 34% over Q-learning with the \\uppaal model, and 72% over Rule-Based Control (RBC). Our method, MPC Q-learning, dynamically incorporates weather conditions, outperforming other Q-learning approaches.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kim, Esther Hahyeon","Nielsen, Thomas Dyhre","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Goorden, Martijn","Ghaffari, Mohsen","Wasowski, Andrzej","Høeg-Petersen, Andreas Holck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-743453"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Combined sewer overflows","Control synthesis","Model predictive control","Reinforcement learning","Stormwater management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"minimizing combined sewer overflows with online model predictive reinforcement learning","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"funding_acknowledgement":["DIREC - Innovation fund"],"id":"S01-000.00-743453","ids":["aau-ff1fe156-5dff-4b3b-849b-1467d8624168"],"keyword":["Combined sewer overflows","Control synthesis","Model predictive control","Reinforcement learning","Stormwater management,"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BC69F708D25763563BE1285CBAAA733A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esther Hahyeon","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","locid":"b5e4baa3-b733-4458-8c7d-e2cafa731be9","name":"Kim, Esther Hahyeon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Dyhre","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d815ae40-14ed-44a2-a215-172e83022c8e","name":"Nielsen, Thomas Dyhre","orcid":"0000-0002-4823-6341","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Guldstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martijn","key":"goordenpau","last":"Goorden","locid":"d71e2c9c-86de-43d9-b98b-2d204bd7a9fa","name":"Goorden, Martijn","orcid":"0000-0002-0641-7240","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas Holck","key":"høegpetersenpau","last":"Høeg-Petersen","locid":"c4ec89d5-fd6a-4cdd-b7a5-9a6415f34f64","name":"Høeg-Petersen, Andreas Holck","orcid":"0009-0003-7829-7318","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Journal - in the process","pages":"1-18","status":"s","title":"Journal - in the process"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","6. Clean Water and Sanitation","9. Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["aau-ff1fe156-5dff-4b3b-849b-1467d8624168"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Minimizing Combined Sewer Overflows with Online Model-Predictive Reinforcement Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743453","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
