,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1a10abd-9db2-4146-815d-57736cc40085"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Formal Specification of Reinforcement Learning","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718913","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"To manage the propagation of infectious diseases, particularly fast-spreading pandemics, it is necessary to provide information about possible infected places and individuals, however, it needs diagnostic tests and is time-consuming and expensive. To smooth these issues, and motivated by the current Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) pandemic, in this paper, we propose a learning-based system and a hidden Markov model (i) to assess hazardous places of a contagious disease, and (ii) to predict the probability of individuals’ infection. To this end, we track the trajectories of individuals in an environment. For evaluating the models and the approaches, we use the Covid-19 outbreak in an urban environment as a case study. Individuals in a closed population are explicitly represented by their movement trajectories over a period of time. The simulation results demonstrate that by adjusting the communicable disease parameters, the detector system and the predictor system are able to correctly assess the hazardous places and determine the infection possibility of individuals and cluster them accurately with high probability, i.e., on average more than 96%. In general, the proposed approaches to assessing hazardous places and predicting the infection possibility of individuals can be applied to contagious diseases by tailoring them to the influential features of the disease.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Davoodi Monfared, Mansour","Ghaffari, Mohsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718823"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Center for Advanced System Understanding (CASUS)","Helmholtz-Zentrum Dresden-Rossendorf","Institute for Advanced Studies in Basic Sciences"],"keyword":["Covid 19","Hidden Markov model","Machine learning","Patient prediction","Trajectory clustering","Trajectory tracking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learning based systems for assessing hazard places of contagious diseases and diagnosing patient possibility","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102802770/PublDoc-22582.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718823","identifier":[{"id":"85140492430","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-065e3d5c-303e-4d49-b829-d42cdd998742"],"keyword":["Covid-19","Hidden Markov model;","Machine learning;","Patient prediction;","Trajectory clustering","Trajectory tracking;"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D717567869296539BC7A79026E28EA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102802770/PublDoc-22582.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.hzdr.de/db/!Publications?pNid=head&pSelMenu=0&pSelTitle=35381","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ir","key":"institute for advanced studies in basic sciences","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Institute for Advanced Studies in Basic Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"center for advanced system understanding","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Center for Advanced System Understanding (CASUS)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"helmholtz zentrum dresden rossendorf","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz-Zentrum Dresden-Rossendorf","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mansour","key":"davoodimonfaredpau","last":"Davoodi Monfared","name":"Davoodi Monfared, Mansour","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","locid":"c12518ce-b3ab-469c-81fb-e2178e6b87e3","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","orcid":"0000-0002-1939-9053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eswa.2022.119043","issn":["09574174","18736793"],"issn_org":["09574174"],"issue":"Part B","journal":"Expert Systems with Applications","paperid":"119043","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Expert Systems with Applications","title_org":"Expert Systems With Applications","volume":"213"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140492430"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-065e3d5c-303e-4d49-b829-d42cdd998742"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Learning-based systems for assessing hazard places of contagious diseases and diagnosing patient possibility","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718823","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The development process for reinforcement learning applications is still exploratory rather than systematic. This exploratory nature reduces reuse of specifications between applications and increases the chances of introducing programming errors. This paper takes a step towards systematizing the development of reinforcement learning applications. We introduce a formal specification of reinforcement learning problems and algorithms, with a particular focus on temporal difference methods and their definitions in backup diagrams. We further develop a test harness for a large class of reinforcement learning applications based on temporal difference learning, including SARSA and Q-learning. The entire development is rooted in functional programming methods; starting with pure specifications and denotational semantics, ending with property-based testing and using compositional interpreters for a domain-specific term language as a test oracle for concrete implementations. We demonstrate the usefulness of this testing method on a number of examples, and evaluate with mutation testing. We show that our test suite is effective in killing mutants (90% mutants killed for 75% of subject agents). More importantly, almost half of all mutants are killed by generic write-once-use-everywhere tests that apply to any reinforcement learning problem modeled using our library, without any additional effort from the programmer.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Varshosaz, Mahsa","Ghaffari, Mohsen","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718929"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Program specifications","Software testing and debugging","Theory of computation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formal specification and testing for reinforcement learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3607835","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718929","identifier":[{"id":"85170641997","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e1a419da-e1e2-4370-82df-ef6d760dcef4"],"keyword":["Program specifications","Software testing and debugging","Theory of computation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57A3A50D8022ABBDAEC486C17E7459DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3607835","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102788488/23-icfp.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","locid":"c12518ce-b3ab-469c-81fb-e2178e6b87e3","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","orcid":"0000-0002-1939-9053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3607835","issn":["24751421"],"issue":"Issue ICFP","journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","pages":"125-158","paperid":"193","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"7"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170641997"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e1a419da-e1e2-4370-82df-ef6d760dcef4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formal Specification and Testing for Reinforcement Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718929","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We provide a simple new randomized contraction approach to the global minimum cut problem for simple undirected graphs. The contractions exploit 2-out edge sampling from each vertex rather than the standard uniform edge sampling. We demonstrate the power of our new approach by obtaining better algorithms for sequential, distributed, and parallel models of computation. Our end results include the following randomized algorithms for computing edge connectivity, with high probability1: • Two sequential algorithms with complexities O(m log n) and O(m + n log3 n). These improve on a long line of developments including a celebrated O(m log3 n) algorithm of Karger [STOC'96] and the state of the art O(m log2 n(log log n)2) algorithm of Henzinger et al. [SODA'17]. Moreover, our O(m + n log3 n) algorithm is optimal when m = Ω(n log3 n). • An Õ(n0.8D0.2 + n0.9) round distributed algorithm, where D denotes the graph diameter. This improves substantially on a recent breakthrough of Daga et al.[STOC'19], which achieved a round complexity of Õ(n1−1/353D1/353 + n1−1/706), hence providing the first sublinear distributed algorithm for exactly computing the edge connectivity. • The first O(1) round algorithm for the massively parallel computation setting with linear memory per machine.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ghaffari, Mohsen","Nowicki, Krzysztof","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477105"],"event":{"acronym":"SODA","end":"2020-01-08","place":"Salt Lake City, us","start":"2020-01-05","title":"31st Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"faster algorithms for edge connectivity via random 000000000002 out contractions","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85084036820&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-477105","identifier":[{"id":"85084036820","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8bf49663-098a-4b71-a383-0a7e7b9d7835"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-4A8CD33F5F8D7F95DA096A62DA431081"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Krzysztof","key":"nowickipau","last":"Nowicki","locid":"d1e7c7e9-e142-4052-b491-5de7b1eae1fc","name":"Nowicki, Krzysztof","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"9a753f32-9b71-4058-8b1e-a94b71903f10","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5237-1709","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shuchi","key":"chawlapedh","last":"Chawla","name":"Chawla, Shuchi","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611975994.77","eisbn":["9781611975994"],"pages":"1260-1279","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"31st Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084036820"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8bf49663-098a-4b71-a3